From 58a61ebf7738cfddc56483fa99f00065543d2cdb Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: daveey <daveey@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Fri, 30 Oct 2026 10:05:53 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] fix(gateway): reap SIGKILLed gateways' stale hermes-gw-*
 fallback dirs; test fixtures stop children with SIGTERM [daveey]

A gateway killed with SIGKILL never runs cleanup_files, so its shared-temp
hermes-gw-<hash>/control.sock dir outlived it (5 per tests/gateway/test_session_kanban.py
run on the hub). The next fallback bind now reaps sibling hermes-gw-* dirs that are
provably ours and dead: a real 0700 dir owned by our uid, >10 min old, holding only a
socket that refuses connect (ECONNREFUSED), never our own target, never via symlink,
at most 200 candidates per start.

Test fixtures: local_recovery_probe.daemon() and automation_peer teardown SIGTERM and
wait 10 s before kill(), and TMPDIR passes to children.
